@startuml
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/kcna-theme.puml
title completions and parallelism — how many finish, and how many at once

rectangle "The two fields, in the API's own words" <<group>> as defs {
  rectangle "completions\n<size:11>“the desired number of SUCCESSFULLY FINISHED pods the job should be run with”</size>\n<size:11>a TOTAL across the whole Job — set it to 10 and ten Pods must succeed</size>" <<accent>> as c
  rectangle "parallelism\n<size:11>“the maximum desired number of pods the job should run AT ANY GIVEN TIME”</size>\n<size:11>a CONCURRENCY CAP — set it to 3 and at most three run together</size>" <<good>> as p
  c -right-> p
}

rectangle "1 · Non-parallel\n<size:11>leave BOTH unset — both default to 1</size>\n\n<size:11>[pod] → success</size>\n\n<size:11>one Pod; the Job is complete as soon as it</size>\n<size:11>terminates successfully. A failure is retried,</size>\n<size:11>but only one Pod runs at a time.</size>" <<plain>> as pat1

rectangle "2 · Fixed completion count\n<size:11>completions: 6 · parallelism: 2</size>\n\n<size:11>[pod][pod] → [pod][pod] → [pod][pod]</size>\n\n<size:11>six Pods must succeed, at most two at once —</size>\n<size:11>so three waves. Near the end the controller runs</size>\n<size:11>fewer than parallelism, because only the remaining</size>\n<size:11>completions are left to do.</size>\n<size:11>completionMode: Indexed gives each Pod an index 0..5.</size>" <<accent>> as pat2

rectangle "3 · Work queue\n<size:11>completions UNSET · parallelism: 3</size>\n\n<size:11>[pod][pod][pod] all pulling from a shared queue</size>\n\n<size:11>“the success of ANY pod signals the success of all”.</size>\n<size:11>Once one succeeds, no new Pods are created; the rest</size>\n<size:11>are allowed to finish. The Pods must coordinate</size>\n<size:11>amongst themselves to decide who does what.</size>" <<good>> as pat3

defs -[hidden]down-> pat1
pat1 -right-> pat2
pat2 -right-> pat3

caption <i>parallelism 0 pauses the Job. Actual concurrency can be lower than requested: a fixed-count Job never runs more Pods than it has completions left, quota or permissions can block Pod creation,</i>\n<i>and the controller throttles after repeated failures. Setting completions to null is what makes a Job a work queue — it is not the same as setting it to 1, which caps parallelism at 1 as well.</i>
@enduml
